  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Resilient Agriculture: transforming the livelihoods of 35,342 people in Marsabit County</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to achieve improved livelihoods security for poor women, men and children in Marsabit county, through an integrated approach that:
&#x2022; increases the productivity and resilience of agricultural systems; 
&#x2022; consolidates engagement in markets and diversified income generation; 
&#x2022; strengthens adaptation to climate change;
&#x2022; increases the ability of local, small scale food producers to access services and influence development practices. 

The targeted groups will benefit from increased crop and livestock productivity as a result of understanding and applying climate resilient agricultural practices and management of natural resources, which means they will suffer fewer losses due to climate-related shocks or environmental degradation. With increased food production and nutritional diversity at the household level, there will be year-round food security and reduced incidences of malnutrition.  They will have surplus to sell for household income and they will access fairer prices for products due to having a greater understanding of the market and how to add value, work in producer groups and engage with traders and input suppliers directly.</narrative>
  </description>
